    "trigger_phrase_provenance": "AUTHORED, NOT OBSERVED. CORPUS_DESIGN §3.3.1 describes notice_trigger_phrases as 'verbatim strings observed in real notices'. No real deactivation notice was available when this corpus was built, so every phrase below is derived from published policy wording and carries observed:false. They must be replaced with observed strings as the B10 golden set is labelled; until then they are a hypothesis, not evidence.",
    "thresholds_are_judgment": "CORPUS_DESIGN §3.2 flags severity_band, triage_disposition and the uniform 0.75 classifier_floor as judgment calls with no published benchmark. Calibrate against the golden set (LLM_ENGINE §8.1) before treating any of them as correct.",
    "walmart_taxonomy_is_a_construction": "CORPUS_DESIGN §3.4 — Walmart publishes no enumerated violation taxonomy. The six WMT codes are assembled from the public sibling guides (performance standards, code of conduct, trust & safety, prohibited products, retailer policies) and are flagged constructed:true."
